<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ngo Dinh Diem</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1901">1901</a>–<a href="/years/1963">1963</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ngo Dinh Diem was a Vietnamese Catholic nationalist who became prime minister of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-vietnam">State of Vietnam</a> in 1954. In 1955 he deposed the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai">Bao Dai</a> through a referendum and proclaimed the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> in the south, ruling as its first president with American support. His repression of Buddhists provoked crisis, and he was killed in a military coup in November 1963.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ngo-dinh-diem.jpg" alt="Ngo Dinh Diem" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Press and Information Office, Embassy of the Republic of Vietnam, Washington, D.C. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:President_NGO-DINH-DIEM_of_the_Republic_of_Viet-Nam.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
